{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in small deterministic specifications. The policy is coverage-biased in clear space, uses one-shot directed recovery after obstacle events, reserves backward motion only for front-obstacle escape, and returns to forward exploration immediately when path_clear is observed. Action states self-loop on path_clear so open-loop pulses are not preempted, while safety-critical obstacle events redirect to recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability with two plant automata",
    "Use one policy specification to map sensed conditions to exactly one allowed controllable action per mode, with short one-shot recovery and fast return to forward exploration"
  ],
